{'symbol': 'FSLR', 'date': '2021-06-09 09:01:00', 'title': 'FIRST SOLAR TO INVEST $680M IN EXPANDING AMERICAN SOLAR MANUFACTURING CAPACITY BY 3.3 GW', 'text': "TEMPE, ARIZ., JUNE 09, 2021 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- FIRST SOLAR, INC. (NASDAQ: FSLR) TODAY ANNOUNCED THAT IT WILL INVEST $680 MILLION TO EXPAND AMERICA'S DOMESTIC PHOTOVOLTAIC (PV) SOLAR MANUFACTURING CAPACITY BY 3.3 GIGAWATTS (GW)DC ANNUALLY, REPRESENTING AN IMPLIED CAPITAL EXPENDITURE OF APPROXIMATELY $0.20 PER WATT. THE COMPANY INTENDS TO FUND CONSTRUCTION OF ITS THIRD US MANUFACTURING FACILITY, IN LAKE TOWNSHIP, OHIO, WITH EXISTING CASH RESOURCES."}